From 0c4c819fdab440bb666db0185e7602b614a8155a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:02:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Update a running install to a trusted commit, verify it after
 restart, roll it back (H624 partial)

The owner pins trust once through an irreversible-tier card (hub.update_trust): SSH signing
keys in Nerva's own allowed-signers file, OpenPGP keys in a dedicated keyring whose primary
fingerprints must equal the declared ones, or one pinned commit. With no trust every apply is
refused. Verification runs git isolated from the global and system config with the signing
programs fixed, so the repository cannot pick what runs.

`plan` lists commits, files, the lock change, migration-shaped files, versions, the verdict and
every refusal. A hub.update card, accepted by a person with its payload unchanged, re-checks,
takes and verifies a full backup, writes a receipt, fast-forwards to the verified sha, installs
requirements-beta.lock hash-pinned and wheels-only when it changed, and restarts through
hub_restart. The restarted hub checks /readyz, its boot commit and version, and on failure
returns to the previous commit (old lock, backup staged when a migration may have run) and
restarts; serve.py rolls back code that never starts. Rollback of the last update is a
hub.update_rollback card, or an offline command with the hub stopped.

Admin routes GET /api/admin/ops/update/{plan,receipts}, POST /api/admin/ops/update/{apply,
rollback,trust}; `nerva update status|plan|apply|rollback|trust`; the Restart / Update panel
plans, requests the update and the rollback. Snapshots, schema, sweep, HUD bundle, Hermes
records and docs regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
